[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m ### Step 1: Convert numbers to base 10
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m First, understand what $ 17_b $ and $ 97_b $ represent in base 10:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m So, the problem asks for values of $ b > 9 $ such that $ b + 7 $ divides $ 9b + 7 $. In other words, we want integers $ b > 9 $ such that $ b + 7 \mid 9b + 7 $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
