[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m Let’s go through the combinations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m #### Case 1: $ b = 0 $ (No 7s)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m We compute $ 3^a $ for $ a = 0 $ to $ 4 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 0 \Rightarrow 1 \Rightarrow 1 \mod 10 = 1 $ ✅
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 1 \Rightarrow 3 \Rightarrow 3 \mod 10 = 3 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 2 \Rightarrow 9 \Rightarrow 9 \mod 10 = 9 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 3 \Rightarrow 27 \Rightarrow 7 \mod 10 = 7 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 4 \Rightarrow 81 \Rightarrow 1 \mod 10 = 1 $ ✅
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m So from this case, the valid numbers are: **1** and **81**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m #### Case 2: $ b = 1 $ (Include 7)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m Now compute $ 3^a \cdot 7 $ for $ a = 0 $ to $ 4 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 0 \Rightarrow 7 \Rightarrow 7 \mod 10 = 7 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 1 \Rightarrow 3 \cdot 7 = 21 \Rightarrow 1 \mod 10 = 1 $ ✅
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 2 \Rightarrow 9 \cdot 7 = 63 \Rightarrow 3 \mod 10 = 3 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 3 \Rightarrow 27 \cdot 7 = 189 \Rightarrow 9 \mod 10 = 9 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m - $ a = 4 \Rightarrow 81 \cdot 7 = 567 \Rightarrow 7 \mod 10 = 7 $ ❌
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m So from this case, the valid number is: **21**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m ### Step 4: Collect and Sum Valid Numbers
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m The valid numbers ending in 1 and dividing $ 9! $ are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=274509)[0m 
